                <pb facs="0898" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg778"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Eddy to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Eddy reports that no disturbances have taken place in this city during the
                    last twenty-four hours. The disturbances are apparently over, and it is believed
                    that the railways will be put in operation early next week.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
